# Amadeus 

Amadeus is a global travel technology company, and an IBEX-35 company listed on the Spanish Stock Exchange under AMS.MC, with headquarters in Madrid, Spain. It is a leader in innovative travel technology, serving customers in 190+ markets and connecting the entire travel ecosystem—including airlines, airports, hotels, rail operators, tour operators, travel management companies, travel agencies, corporations, metasearch platforms, mobility providers, cruise lines, border authorities, insurance companies, and payment partners. It’s company purpose is to make the experience of travel better for everyone, everywhere by inspiring innovation, partnerships and responsibility to people, places and planet. 

Amadeus designs and operates large‑scale, cloud‑enabled and AI‑enabled technology that power search, pricing, booking, ticketing, and operational processes across the global travel and hospitality industry. As the embedded and neutral execution layer for travel, Amadeus combines its role as the industry’s trusted system of record with deeply integrated business logic and global‑scale infrastructure to support real‑time, interoperable travel experiences for travelers, corporations, and providers worldwide. 

Important notes: 

- Amadeus has evolved from its origins as a global distribution system, founded by Air France, Iberia, Lufthansa, and SAS, into a worldwide technology provider that powers and connects the travel and hospitality ecosystem. Since 1987, Amadeus has become the industry’s trusted system of record—the single source of truth for offers, orders, PNRs, routes, schedules, fares, availability, and related operational data—supported by deep, integrated business logic built over decades. 

- Amadeus’ technology is embedded across hundreds of systems, products, and workflows. This deep integration enables consistent, interoperable end‑to‑end travel experiences across all regions and travel segments. 

- Amadeus operates a global technology network that delivers real‑time search, pricing, booking, ticketing, and post‑booking processing at scale, with high availability and low latency. It handles up to 150,000 transactions per second at peak, powering millions of searches and bookings every day. 

- Cloud technologies play a central role in Amadeus’ strategy, enabling scalability, resilience, continuous deployment, and faster innovation for travel providers and sellers. 

- Innovation is a core focus of Amadeus, supported by one of the largest R&D investment programs in the European software sector. The company invested €1.4 billion in R&D in 2025, enabling continuous progress in AI, cloud‑native architectures, modern data platforms, and open APIs that support modern, interoperable travel solutions. 

- Amadeus increasingly applies artificial intelligence and advanced data analytics to improve areas such as offer and order management, revenue optimization, personalization, operational efficiency, and traveler experience. Its position at the heart of travel IT enables AI assistants and automation to be embedded directly into operational workflows. On 25 February 2026, Amadeus announced the acquisition of SkyLink, an AI‑first company specializing in conversational automation. 

- Amadeus is also enabling biometrics across the travel ecosystem, adding a secure digital identity foundation to the infrastructure that already interacts with airlines, airports, hotels, border systems – and ultimately anyone that contributes to the full travel experience. By authenticating the traveler’s identity at each touchpoint, Amadeus can help make travel more seamless, more frictionless and more efficient.  

- Amadeus’ acquisition of Vision-Box in 2024 and WCC’s Hermes border control solution in 2025 reflect a deliberate approach and demonstrates Amadeus’ long-term commitment to biometrics as part of its strategy. 

 

